    {
      "id": 11,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Por eso,"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "el duque"},
        {"t": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "lo envió a mi colegio."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "por, a causa de", "base": "because of", "sense": "cause"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "esto"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "el duque", "base": "duke", "sense": "noble"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "envió", "base": "send", "sense": "dispatch"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "lo, a él"},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9], "es": "a mi colegio", "base": "school", "sense": "education"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 12,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "Y después de dos semanas"},
        {"t": [4, 5], "es": "con nosotros,"},
        {"t": [6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "estaba mucho más contento."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [1, 3], "es": "después de semanas", "base": "week", "sense": "time"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "dos"},
        {"t": [4, 5], "es": "con nosotros"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "estaba", "base": "be", "sense": "state"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "mucho", "base": "much", "sense": "degree", "note": "Para reforzar un comparativo se usa *much*, no *very*: *much happier* = «mucho más contento» ([[comparatives]])."},
        {"t": [9], "es": "más contento", "base": "happy", "sense": "feeling", "note": "El final *-er* forma el comparativo. La *y* de *happy* cambia a *i*: *happier* ([[comparatives]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 13,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "«Entonces,"},
        {"t": [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], "es": "la noche del trece de mayo,"},
        {"t": [9, 10], "es": "desapareció."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "entonces", "base": "then", "sense": "next"},
        {"t": [1, 2, 3], "es": "en la noche", "base": "night", "sense": "time"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6], "es": "del día trece", "note": "En las fechas inglesas se usan números ordinales: *13th* se lee *thirteenth* ([[ordinal-dates]])."},
        {"t": [7, 8], "es": "de mayo", "note": "En inglés, los meses se escriben con mayúscula: *May*."},
        {"t": [9], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [10], "es": "desapareció", "base": "disappear", "sense": "vanish"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 14,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], "es": "Para llegar a su dormitorio"},
        {"t": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "hay que pasar por otra habitación más grande."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "el camino, el acceso", "base": "way", "sense": "path"},
        {"t": [2, 3, 4], "es": "a su dormitorio", "base": "bedroom", "sense": "room"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "es", "base": "be", "sense": "identity", "note": "Aquí, *the way is through* indica por dónde se pasa: «para llegar hay que pasar por»."},
        {"t": [6, 7, 9], "es": "por otra habitación", "base": "room", "sense": "building", "note": "*Through* indica que atraviesas el interior de algo: entras por un lado y sales por otro."},
        {"t": [8], "es": "más grande", "base": "large", "sense": "size", "note": "El final *-er* forma el comparativo: *larger* = «más grande» ([[comparatives]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 15,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Dos chicos mayores"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "duermen allí."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "dos"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "mayores", "base": "old", "sense": "age", "note": "*Older* compara edades: «mayores», no «viejos». El final *-er* forma el comparativo ([[comparatives]])."},
        {"t": [2], "es": "niños", "base": "boy", "sense": "child"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "duermen", "base": "sleep", "sense": "rest"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "allí", "base": "there", "sense": "place"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 16,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Uno de ellos"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "nunca duerme muy bien,"},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9, 10, 11, 12], "es": "y no oyó ni vio nada"},
        {"t": [13, 14], "es": "aquella noche."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "uno"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "de ellos"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "nunca", "base": "never", "sense": "time", "note": "*Never* ya hace negativa la frase: no se añade *not*, aunque en español puedas decir «no… nunca» ([[negative-words]])."},
        {"t": [4], "es": "duerme", "base": "sleep", "sense": "rest"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "muy", "base": "very", "sense": "degree"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "bien", "base": "well", "sense": "manner"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [9], "es": "oyó", "base": "hear", "sense": "sound"},
        {"t": [10], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [11], "es": "vio", "base": "see", "sense": "sight"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "nada", "note": "*Nothing* ya niega la frase: el inglés no añade *not*. Por eso *heard nothing* es «no oyó nada» ([[negative-words]])."},
        {"t": [13, 14], "es": "aquella noche", "base": "night", "sense": "time"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 17,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "Así que"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "el joven Arthur"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "no salió"},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9], "es": "por esa habitación."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "así que", "base": "so", "sense": "result"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "joven", "base": "young", "sense": "age"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "Arthur"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "no salió", "base": "go out", "sense": "leave", "note": "*Did not* forma la negación en pasado. *Go* queda en su forma base ([[auxiliary-do]])."},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9], "es": "por esa habitación", "base": "room", "sense": "building", "note": "*Through* indica que se atraviesa un lugar por dentro, no que se pasa cerca."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 18,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "Su ventana"},
        {"t": [2, 3], "es": "estaba abierta,"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7], "es": "y hay hiedra"},
        {"t": [8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14], "es": "por toda la pared de la casa, hasta arriba."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "su ventana", "base": "window", "sense": "opening"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "estaba", "base": "be", "sense": "state"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "abierta", "base": "open", "sense": "unclosed"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [5, 6], "es": "hay", "base": "be", "sense": "exist", "note": "*There is* presenta algo que hay. Aquí *there* no significa «allí» ([[dummy-subject]])."},
        {"t": [7], "es": "hiedra", "base": "ivy", "sense": "plant"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "por completo", "base": "all", "sense": "extent"},
        {"t": [9, 10, 11], "es": "por la pared, hacia arriba", "base": "wall", "sense": "building", "note": "*Up* indica dirección hacia arriba: la hiedra sube por la pared. *All up* añade que llega hasta arriba."},
        {"t": [12, 13, 14], "es": "de la casa", "base": "house", "sense": "building"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 19,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Es fácil"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], "es": "salir por la ventana"},
        {"t": [9, 10, 11, 12], "es": "y bajar por la hiedra"},
        {"t": [13, 14, 15], "es": "hasta el suelo."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "(no se traduce)", "note": "El inglés necesita un sujeto: *it* no se refiere a ninguna cosa. La idea viene después: salir y bajar ([[dummy-subject]])."},
        {"t": [1], "es": "es", "base": "be", "sense": "identity"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "fácil", "base": "easy", "sense": "simple"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "salir de", "base": "get out of", "sense": "leave", "note": "*Get out of* expresa salir de un lugar. Aquí, en español decimos «salir por la ventana» ([[phrasal-verbs]])."},
        {"t": [7, 8], "es": "la ventana", "base": "window", "sense": "opening"},
        {"t": [9], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [10, 11, 12], "es": "por la hiedra, hacia abajo", "base": "ivy", "sense": "plant", "note": "Se sobreentiende el movimiento de *get*: *down the ivy* indica bajar por la hiedra."},
        {"t": [13, 14, 15], "es": "hasta el suelo", "base": "ground", "sense": "surface"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 20,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Así que creemos"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 8], "es": "que salió por ahí."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "así que", "base": "so", "sense": "result"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "creemos", "base": "think", "sense": "believe"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "que"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [5, 6], "es": "salió", "base": "go out", "sense": "leave", "note": "*Out* añade la idea de salir al exterior: no es solo ir a otro sitio ([[phrasal-verbs]])."},
        {"t": [7, 8], "es": "por ese camino", "base": "way", "sense": "path"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 21,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "«Llevaba su ropa habitual del colegio,"},
        {"t": [7, 8], "es": "creemos:"},
        {"t": [10, 11, 12, 13], "es": "una chaqueta negra corta"},
        {"t": [14, 15, 16, 17], "es": "y unos pantalones azul oscuro."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "llevaba", "base": "be", "sense": "state", "note": "*Be in* seguido de ropa indica qué lleva alguien puesto: *in his coat* = «con su chaqueta»."},
        {"t": [3, 6], "es": "sus prendas", "base": "thing", "sense": "belongings", "note": "*Things* puede referirse a prendas de ropa, no solo a objetos."},
        {"t": [4], "es": "habituales", "base": "usual", "sense": "normal"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "del colegio", "base": "school", "sense": "education", "note": "*School* describe para qué es la ropa. Un sustantivo delante de otro puede hacer de adjetivo ([[noun-as-adjective]])."},
        {"t": [7], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "creemos", "base": "think", "sense": "believe"},
        {"t": [10, 13], "es": "una chaqueta", "base": "coat", "sense": "clothing"},
        {"t": [11], "es": "corta", "base": "short", "sense": "length"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "negra", "base": "black", "sense": "colour"},
        {"t": [14], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [15], "es": "oscuro", "base": "dark", "sense": "colour"},
        {"t": [16], "es": "azul", "base": "blue", "sense": "colour"},
        {"t": [17], "es": "pantalones", "base": "trousers", "sense": "clothing", "note": "Palabra británica; en EE. UU., *pants* ([[british-american]]). *Trousers* lleva verbo en plural: *the trousers are…* ([[plural-agreement]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 22,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "es": "Revisamos toda su habitación"},
        {"t": [6, 7], "es": "con mucha atención,"},
        {"t": [8, 9, 10], "es": "pero no encontramos"},
        {"t": [11, 12], "es": "nada extraño,"},
        {"t": [13, 14], "es": "nada fuera de lo normal."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "miramos", "base": "look", "sense": "see", "note": "Aquí, «revisamos» suena más natural en español: *all through* indica que miraron por toda la habitación."},
        {"t": [2], "es": "por completo", "base": "all", "sense": "extent"},
        {"t": [3, 4, 5], "es": "por su habitación", "base": "room", "sense": "building"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "muy", "base": "very", "sense": "degree"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "con atención", "base": "carefully", "sense": "attention"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "pero"},
        {"t": [9], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [10], "es": "encontramos", "base": "find", "sense": "discover"},
        {"t": [11], "es": "nada", "note": "*Nothing* ya niega la frase: el inglés no añade *not*. Por eso *found nothing* es «no encontramos nada» ([[negative-words]])."},
        {"t": [12], "es": "extraño", "base": "strange", "sense": "unusual"},
        {"t": [13], "es": "nada"},
        {"t": [14], "es": "inusual, poco común", "base": "unusual", "sense": "uncommon"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 23,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4], "es": "«Cuando me enteré de la noticia"},
        {"t": [5, 6, 7, 8, 9, 10], "es": "a las siete de la mañana del martes,"},
        {"t": [11, 12, 13], "es": "llamé a todo el mundo"},
        {"t": [14, 15, 16, 17], "es": "para que fuera al aula grande."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "cuando"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "yo"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "me enteré de", "base": "learn", "sense": "discover", "note": "En británico es habitual *learnt*; en EE. UU. se prefiere *learned*. Aquí no es estudiar, sino recibir información ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "las noticias", "base": "news", "sense": "information", "note": "Aunque acaba en *-s*, *news* no es plural: es un sustantivo incontable ([[uncountable]])."},
        {"t": [5, 6], "es": "a las siete"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "en punto", "base": "o'clock", "sense": "time"},
        {"t": [8, 9], "es": "el martes", "note": "Con los días se usa *on*: *on Tuesday*. Los días de la semana llevan mayúscula en inglés."},
        {"t": [10], "es": "mañana", "base": "morning", "sense": "time"},
        {"t": [11], "es": "yo"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "llamé", "base": "call", "sense": "call", "note": "Aquí es llamar a alguien para que venga, no hacer una llamada de teléfono."},
        {"t": [13], "es": "todo el mundo"},
        {"t": [14, 15, 17], "es": "al aula", "base": "schoolroom", "sense": "classroom", "note": "*Into* indica movimiento hacia dentro; *in* indica dónde está algo."},
        {"t": [16], "es": "grande", "base": "big", "sense": "size"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 24,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5], "es": "Entonces nos enteramos de más malas noticias:"},
        {"t": [7, 8, 9, 10], "es": "Heidegger, el profesor de alemán,"},
        {"t": [11, 12, 13], "es": "también había desaparecido."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "entonces", "base": "then", "sense": "next"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "nos enteramos de", "base": "learn", "sense": "discover", "note": "En británico es habitual *learnt*; en EE. UU. se prefiere *learned*. Aquí no es estudiar, sino recibir información ([[british-american]])."},
        {"t": [3], "es": "más", "base": "more", "sense": "quantity"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "malas", "base": "bad", "sense": "quality"},
        {"t": [5], "es": "noticias", "base": "news", "sense": "information", "note": "Aunque acaba en *-s*, *news* no es plural: es un sustantivo incontable ([[uncountable]])."},
        {"t": [7], "es": "Heidegger"},
        {"t": [8, 10], "es": "el profesor", "base": "teacher", "sense": "person"},
        {"t": [9], "es": "de alemán", "base": "German", "sense": "language", "note": "En *German teacher*, *German* indica la materia ([[noun-as-adjective]]). Los idiomas llevan mayúscula."},
        {"t": [11], "es": "estaba", "base": "be", "sense": "state"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "desaparecido", "base": "missing", "sense": "lost", "note": "Con *be*, *missing* describe un estado: es un adjetivo, no una acción en curso ([[linking-verbs]])."},
        {"t": [13], "es": "también", "base": "too", "sense": "also"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 25,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "Su habitación"},
        {"t": [2, 3, 4], "es": "no está lejos"},
        {"t": [5, 6, 7], "es": "de la de Arthur."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0, 1], "es": "su habitación", "base": "room", "sense": "building"},
        {"t": [2, 3], "es": "no está", "base": "be", "sense": "state"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "lejos", "base": "far", "sense": "distance"},
        {"t": [5, 7], "es": "de la habitación", "base": "room", "sense": "building"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "de Arthur", "note": "El *’s* indica de quién es algo: *Arthur’s room* = «la habitación de Arthur» ([[possessive-s]])."}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 26,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2], "es": "Heidegger bajó"},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "por la hiedra:"},
        {"t": [6, 7, 8], "es": "lo sabemos"},
        {"t": [9, 10, 11, 12, 13], "es": "porque encontramos sus huellas"},
        {"t": [14, 15, 16], "es": "en el suelo,"},
        {"t": [17, 18, 19], "es": "debajo de la ventana."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "Heidegger"},
        {"t": [1, 2], "es": "bajó", "base": "go down", "sense": "lower", "note": "*Down* añade dirección hacia abajo al movimiento de *go* ([[phrasal-verbs]])."},
        {"t": [3, 4], "es": "la hiedra", "base": "ivy", "sense": "plant"},
        {"t": [6], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [7], "es": "sabemos", "base": "know", "sense": "information"},
        {"t": [8], "es": "esto"},
        {"t": [9], "es": "porque"},
        {"t": [10], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [11], "es": "encontramos", "base": "find", "sense": "discover"},
        {"t": [12, 13], "es": "sus huellas", "base": "footprint", "sense": "mark", "note": "Son huellas de pies: *foot* es «pie» y *print*, una marca que algo deja."},
        {"t": [14, 15, 16], "es": "en el suelo", "base": "ground", "sense": "surface"},
        {"t": [17, 18, 19], "es": "debajo de la ventana", "base": "window", "sense": "opening"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 27,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3], "es": "También sabemos que"},
        {"t": [4, 5, 6, 7, 8, 9], "es": "solo llevaba la chaqueta,"},
        {"t": [10, 11, 12], "es": "los pantalones y los zapatos,"},
        {"t": [13, 14, 15, 16, 17], "es": "porque encontramos su camisa"},
        {"t": [18, 19, 20], "es": "y sus calcetines"},
        {"t": [21, 22, 23, 24, 25, 26], "es": "en el suelo de su habitación."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "sabemos", "base": "know", "sense": "information"},
        {"t": [2], "es": "también", "base": "too", "sense": "also"},
        {"t": [3], "es": "que"},
        {"t": [4], "es": "él"},
        {"t": [5, 7], "es": "llevaba", "base": "be", "sense": "state", "note": "*Be in* seguido de ropa indica qué lleva alguien puesto: *in his coat* = «con su chaqueta»."},
        {"t": [6], "es": "solo", "base": "only", "sense": "just"},
        {"t": [8, 9], "es": "su chaqueta", "base": "coat", "sense": "clothing", "note": "El inglés usa posesivos con la ropa y las partes del cuerpo: *his coat*, *his back* ([[body-possessive]])."},
        {"t": [10], "es": "pantalones", "base": "trousers", "sense": "clothing", "note": "Palabra británica; en EE. UU., *pants* ([[british-american]]). *Trousers* lleva verbo en plural: *the trousers are…* ([[plural-agreement]])."},
        {"t": [11], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [12], "es": "zapatos", "base": "shoe", "sense": "clothing"},
        {"t": [13], "es": "porque"},
        {"t": [14], "es": "nosotros"},
        {"t": [15], "es": "encontramos", "base": "find", "sense": "discover"},
        {"t": [16, 17], "es": "su camisa", "base": "shirt", "sense": "clothing"},
        {"t": [18], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [19, 20], "es": "sus calcetines", "base": "sock", "sense": "clothing"},
        {"t": [21, 22, 23], "es": "en el suelo", "base": "floor", "sense": "surface", "note": "*Floor* es el suelo de una habitación; *ground*, el terreno que pisas al aire libre."},
        {"t": [24, 25, 26], "es": "de su habitación", "base": "room", "sense": "building"}
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": 28,
      "line": [
        {"t": [0, 1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6], "es": "Y se llevó su bicicleta."}
      ],
      "words": [
        {"t": [0], "es": "y"},
        {"t": [1], "es": "él"},
